{"type":"text","timestamp":1794967969288,"sessionID":"ses_e1392fa3dffeOtzqaUmxyl42ww","part":{"id":"prt_1ec6d8ef9002YeEsjSIVx7hD12","sessionID":"ses_e1392fa3dffeOtzqaUmxyl42ww","messageID":"msg_1ec6d8559001P0IasmtFXflpYt","type":"text","text":"Fixed and verified.\n\n## The bug\n\n`calc.py` had `add` subtracting instead of adding:\n\n```python\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a - b      # subtracted, so add(2, 3) returned -1\n```\n\n## The fix\n\nOne line in `/tmp/opencode/oc/proj/r1-tools/calc.py`:\n\n```diff\n def add(a, b):\n-    return a - b\n+    return a + b\n```\n\n`mul` was already correct, so `test_mul` passed before and after — the only failure was `test_add` (`assert -1 == 5`).\n\n## Test results\n\nBefore:\n```\nF.                                                       [100%]\nFAILED test_calc.py::test_add - assert -1 == 5\n1 failed, 1 passed in 0.01s\n```\n\nAfter (`python -m pytest -q`):\n```\n..                                                       [100%]\n2 passed in 0.00s\n```\n\nNote: `notes.txt` in the repo is ~390 KB of generated filler data (\"line N: the value of item N is…\") with no references to the calculator — it isn't involved in the failure. The untracked `__pycache__/` directory is just pytest build output; you may want to gitignore it.","time":{"start":1794967965433,"end":1794967969288}}}
